00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
russian president vladimir putin's first  face-to-face meeting with a nato leader  since russia's invasion of ukraine in  february putin and turkish president  recep tayyip erdogan were in iran's  capital tehran to discuss a unbacked  proposal to resume exports of ukrainian  grain through the black sea to help ease  the global food crisis  i want to thank you for your efforts in  mediation providing a forum for  negotiation on food problems on the  problem of grain export by the black sea  we moved forward under your mediation  not all the problems have been resolved  yet but it's already good that there is  a movement  on his second international trip since  the start of the war in ukraine putin  also met iranian president ibrahim raisi  who hosted the trilateral summit  both russia and iran are among the most  sanctioned countries in the world and  the two nations are now seeking to boost  economic cooperation  this level of business and trade between  the two countries is definitely not  enough considering the existing  capacities and it can go to a higher  level we think we can reach 30 billion  dollars which is three times more than  the current number  just before putin's visit russian energy  giant gazprom and iran's national oil  company signed a memorandum of  understanding worth 40 billion dollars  to develop a gas field around kish  island in the gulf  this summit is a part of astana format a  mechanism that was established five  years ago between russia turkey and iran  to end the 11 year war in syria  while russia and iran are the main  backers of the syrian government led by  bashar al-assad turkey has effectively  supported the syrian opposition  since 2016 turkey has also launched  three major military operations inside  syria against kurdish armed group ypg  and isis  and ankara says preparations are now on  the way to conduct a fourth operation  into syria to create a 30 kilometer deep  security zone a plan that both russia  and iran oppose  but the turkish president did not back  down  milligrams  we are determined to drive out the  centers of evil from syria that threaten  our national security  as astana guarantors our expectation  from the russian federation and iran is  to support turkey in this fight  despite this all three presidents said  the astana peace process has been  effective in setting up a foundation for  peace in syria  russia has withdrawn most of his forces  from syria after the war began in  ukraine now syria is increasingly  becoming a source of tension between  turkey and iran as they both have a  significant military presence in the  country the next round of the trilateral  summit under astana format will be held  in moscow but the fragile balance  between these three countries could  possibly be disturbed in case of a  military operation into syria unless  they can find a diplomatic solution to  the crisis rasul sardar al-jazeera terra
 

